        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 341.22,
          "end": 343.53,
          "en": "not other lists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 343.53,
          "end": 347.67,
          "en": "So converting our answers to AnswerButtons is not enough",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 347.67,
          "end": 350.25,
          "en": "if there is still in a list thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 350.25,
          "end": 352.89,
          "en": "Instead, what we have to do here is something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 352.89,
          "end": 354.87,
          "en": "called spreading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 354.87,
          "end": 358.17,
          "en": "We have to spread this list or this iterable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 358.17,
          "end": 360.3,
          "en": "which is generated by map,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 360.3,
          "end": 363.48,
          "en": "into a couple of individual values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 363.48,
          "end": 367.17,
          "en": "And that's done by adding three dots in front of this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 367.17,
          "end": 368.4,
          "en": "which might look strange",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 368.4,
          "end": 371.34,
          "en": "but which is another built-in operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 371.34,
          "end": 375.303,
          "en": "a built-in keyword you could say which is available in Dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 376.74,
          "end": 380.55,
          "en": "And these three dots will simply take all the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 380.55,
          "end": 382.71,
          "en": "in a list or an iterable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 382.71,
          "end": 384.66,
          "en": "and pull them out of the list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 384.66,
          "end": 386.7,
          "en": "pull them out of the iterable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 386.7,
          "end": 390.42,
          "en": "and instead place them as comma separated values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 390.42,
          "end": 392.373,
          "en": "in this place in code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 393.21,
          "end": 395.67,
          "en": "So now these AnswerButtons in this list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 395.67,
          "end": 397.95,
          "en": "of AnswerButtons here are pulled out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 397.95,
